"Glyphs are found, not invented: the augera made them and set their meanings."
"All glyphs are woven into the augera; the Basic Set sits at their fringes."
"The Special Set sits nearer the augera's essence than the Basic or Advanced Sets."
"To the augera, glyphs are \"descriptions of our nature, shadows of our light\"."
"Glyphs are channels etched for the augera's streams; free the augera and glyphs may fail."
"Glyphs are a standardised form of limited frameshifting, with the mind as the instrument."
"Glyphs let laypeople use arcana without theory, but they narrow what is possible."
"Arcanophany is a framework built by people and the Fateweavers, not an objective truth."
"Oblivion glyphs are multi-dimensional; scribing one needs arcana applied in oblivion too."
"Esoteric glyphs need anchors in higher dimensions, not only in physical matter."
"A glyph scribed in oblivion alone falls apart for want of an anchor; only augera manage it."
"Ordinary parentheses fail on oblivion glyphs and must be extended into oblivion by hand."
"Wysana-making glyphs lie beyond the Special Set and show none of its malleability."
"The wysana preparatory space binds a shape in oblivion to a physical anchor."
"One wysana glyph is a signpost pointing to part of its maker's flare."
"Some glyphs are folded under others and are seen only by folding one's mind."
"No one can read a folded glyph and its unfolded form at the same time."
"Each alien glyph is several glyphs layered into ever higher reaches of reality."
"Some glyphs' true figures include loops of arcana flow; a paper copy is a pale imitation."
"The augera can unfold reality for another, as one thumbs through the pages of a book."
"A glyph for prophetic links exists; it is not public, and Advanced Set users cannot read it."
"Merely looking at the prophetic-links glyph gives the soul a senseless nudge."
"Thinking with a glyph lets one grasp and even sense its concept."
"Prophetic links cannot be vented or frameshifted away; they must be named with their glyph."
"An anti-prophecy shield joins general auric and ambient glyphs to prophetic links, excluded."
"Glyphs give a prophecy's words weight; with the Spires they make it quasi-intelligent."
"The glyph for passing knowledge sits hidden among folded glyphs, like a lock."
"Spire floors bear gold glyphs outside the known sets that hold the augera's crystal aloft."
"Hidden Academy buildings are folded into higher dimensions; their glyphs only warp perception."
"Nightwatchers learn by rote an ultimate defence built from glyphs of sets no one else knows."
"Augera can plant glyphs in a mind, and the bearer can carve them without understanding them."
"Special sequences keyed to flare shapes instruct the augeric web, which then acts on them."
